RETROACTIVE LOG — commit 07bb39d, recorded after the fact (the changelog/ convention
was introduced later, in commit 478c817).

File: vUX-spaEngine.js

=======================================================================
Section 1 — boolean data attribute parsing
OLD_SECTION
loadIntoNode = Boolean(element.dataset[hyphenatedToCamel(dataAttributes.loadIntoNode)]);
addToHistory = Boolean(element.dataset[hyphenatedToCamel(dataAttributes.addToHistory)]);
cache = Boolean(cache == null?true:cache);

NEW_SECTION
function parseBooleanAttribute(value){
    //HTML-friendly boolean: "false" and "0" disable, any other value (including bare presence) enables
    return !(value === "false" || value === "0");
}
loadIntoNode = parseBooleanAttribute(element.dataset[hyphenatedToCamel(dataAttributes.loadIntoNode)]);
addToHistory = parseBooleanAttribute(element.dataset[hyphenatedToCamel(dataAttributes.addToHistory)]);
cache = cache == null ? true : parseBooleanAttribute(cache);

REASON
Boolean(string) is true for every non-empty string, so data-*="false" and "0" were
read as true — the cache/addToHistory/loadIntoNode attributes could never be turned
off from markup.

