Section 2 — saveState(): honor the opt-out
OLD_SECTION
function saveState(contents, elementId){

    var routeName   = routeProperties.name;

NEW_SECTION
function saveState(contents, elementId){

    if (!addToHistory) return; //link opted out of history via the addToHistory data attribute

    var routeName   = routeProperties.name;

REASON
The addToHistory flag was read but never enforced — every navigation pushed history
regardless of the attribute.

=======================================================================
Section 3 — getLinkContent(): per-link flag reset
OLD_SECTION
async function getLinkContent(element){

    if (element.dataset[...loadIntoNode] != undefined){

NEW_SECTION
async function getLinkContent(element){

    //reset per-link flags so one link's attributes don't leak into the next navigation
    loadIntoNode = true;
    addToHistory = true;

    if (element.dataset[...loadIntoNode] != undefined){

REASON
The flags are engine-level variables only overwritten when a link declares the
attribute, so one link's opt-out leaked into every subsequent click; they now reset
to their defaults on every navigation.
